      "id": "CVE-2026-85747",
      "aliases": [
        "GHSA-685w-q87j-wqw3"
      ],
      "title": "Distribution: Client `manifests.Get()` does not verify returned content against requested digest",
      "summary": "Distribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.2, registry/client.(*manifests).Get() reads a manifest returned for a digest-pinned request and passes it to distribution.UnmarshalManifest without hashing the body against the requested digest, allowing a malicious or intercepted registry response to substitute attacker-chosen manifest content even when Docker-Content-Digest claims the requested value. The bundled pull-through proxy in registry/proxy/proxymanifeststore.go can cache and re-serve the substituted manifest. This issue is fixed in version 3.1.2.",
      "published_at": "2026-09-23T14:32:01.000Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-10-18T13:38:36.137Z",
      "severity": {
